  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given equation is\r\n$$\r\n3 x^{2}-3 y^{2}-18 x+12 y+2=0\r\n$$\r\nIt can be written as\r\n$\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}\\right)^{2}}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}\\right)^{2}}=1$\r\n$\\begin{aligned} \\text { here, } a &=b=\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}} \\\\ \\therefore \\quad e &=\\sqrt{1+\\frac{b^{2}}{a^{2}}} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{2} \\end{aligned}$\r\n$\\therefore$ Equation of the directrix are\r\n$$\r\nx=3 \\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{13}{6}}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
